{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/y90nupkv","slideIndex":0,"text":"Based on the user-arranged Downloads/Poster Template.pptx. Original header, title, author text, footer, university artwork and separator are preserved. All new and restyled content is in the central white canvas. All twelve original images retain frames, crops and image bytes.\nSources: Report/ResultsDiscussionRevision_2026-11-02, Results and Appendices/results_evidence.tex. Text validation uses the first-principles reader result 94.39% (shown 94.4%) on 1076 original lines, 45747 characters. Writer validation remains 98.08% on 156 lines. Physical text 84.41% and writer 86.41% are unchanged existing scores and are not relabelled as a new scratch-checkpoint physical evaluation. These are different test sets.\nMean absolute length error 0.297 mm across 70 feature-length measurements. Completion time includes generation and physical drawing. The mean of the 25 job-normalised total-time/character values is 2.4285795021 s per character, shown 2.43 s. The character-weighted pooled ratio is 2.1546609403 s/character and is not the statistic displayed. Relative shape score 86.681246% is against natural handwriting variation, not recognition accuracy. Classification latency remains above target. No model, scoring or hardware test rerun."}